From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] terminal: make ch_ESC constexpr

An in-class `static const char` has no out-of-line definition, so any
odr-use (QDebug streams it by const reference) leaves an undefined
reference to Terminal::ch_ESC at link time. C++17 (required by Qt 6)
makes constexpr static data members implicitly inline, which provides
the definition.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/terminal.h
+++ b/terminal.h
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@

 private:
     Q_DISABLE_COPY(Terminal)
-    static const char ch_ESC = 0x1B; //escape
+    static constexpr char ch_ESC = 0x1B; //escape
     static const int maxScrollBackLines = 300;

     void insertAtCursor(QChar c, bool overwriteMode=true, bool advanceCursor=true);
